47	1	3	Schedule on-site witness test — Darnwick Elementary School Array (640 kW, Arvexa PV-750)	**Facility / Site:** Darnwick Elementary School Array (44 Willowvale Avenue, Darnwick, Alleron 21DA; POI: Secondary service — school building main switchgear)\n**Customer / Host:** Darnwick Community School District (Facilities, (612) 555-0621)\n**Checklist Reference:** `Checklist_Darnwick_Elementary.pdf` (`Doc no. COMM-CHK-DARN-ELEM`, Rev 0, dated `06/15/2025`; Field Engineer `M. Halbrook, P.E.`, badge `AFE-1042`)\n**Nameplate Capacity & Class:** `640 kW` AC (Commercial small-scale DER, `500 kW – 1 MW`, `DIS-01 Rev 4` Table 3-1 / Table 5-1 Category 2)\n**Installed Inverter:** `Arvexa PV-750`\n\n### 1. CEL Carriage & Waiver Eligibility Determination (`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §3, §4.1`)\n- **Call on Carriage:** **NOT CARRIED** on current Certified Equipment List `CEL-2025-Q2` (published `04/30/2025`, superseding `CEL-2024-Q4`; `Arvexa PV-750` does not appear on `CEL-2025-Q2` or `CEL-2024-Q4`).\n- **Disposition:** Ineligible for witness-test waiver under `ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §3` (Corollary 2) and `§4.1` (checklist Section 6 was an unverified batch copy-forward, flagged by Evan Solberg on commissioning wiki page `der-program/commissioning/municipal/checklist-darnwick-elementary`). **On-site witness test required prior to Permission to Operate (PTO).**\n\n### 2. Tests to Be Performed and Basis (`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §4.2`)\nTesting shall be conducted on site per **`IEEE 1547.1`** and **`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §4.2`**, covering the requirements of **`DIS-01 Rev 4 §5 (Table 5-1 Category 2)` & `§6`**, **`IEEE 1547-2018 Clause 4`**, and **`DPS-07 Rev 2`**:\n1. **Protective-Function Trip Tests:** On-site verification of under-/over-voltage (`ANSI 27/59`) and under-/over-frequency (`ANSI 81U/81O`) trip pickup thresholds, clearing times, and reconnect delay timing against the approved site protection settings sheet for the `Arvexa PV-750` internal protection profile (Checklist Section 2.1, 2.3, 2.4).\n2. **Anti-Islanding Function Test:** Unintentional islanding / loss-of-utility test per `IEEE 1547.1` confirming the `Arvexa PV-750` ceases to energize and trips within the required `≤ 2.0 s` window (Checklist Section 2.2).\n3. **Voltage and Frequency Ride-Through (VRT / FRT) Verifications:** Verification of programmed voltage and frequency ride-through profiles (Category II per `DIS-01 Rev 4`) and active/reactive power support settings against the approved settings sheet (`DIS-01 Rev 4 §6`).\n\n### 3. Who Performs and Who Witnesses (`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §4.2, §4.3`)\n- **Scheduling / Coordination:** Alleniom Utilities DER Program Commissioning Coordinator schedules the earliest mutually available test date with the customer/commissioning agent and Alleniom witness engineer (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2`).\n- **Performed / Operated By:** Customer (**Darnwick Community School District**) and its qualified **Commissioning Agent / EPC contractor of record** (coordinated with field engineer `M. Halbrook, P.E.`, `AFE-1042`), who supply the written test plan, calibrated test instrumentation, and qualified personnel to operate the equipment (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2`).\n- **Witnessed, Recorded & Dispositioned By:** **Alleniom Utilities Witness Engineer** (**Standards Engineering** — `Evan Solberg` or designated Alleniom witness engineer), who observes on site, records calibrated instrument identifiers and measured values, assigns pass/fail dispositions per test point, and signs and dates the witness test record (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2, §4.3`).\n\n### 4. What Must Be on File First (`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §4.1–§4.3`, `TCS-02 §3.6, §5`)\n- **Prior to Conducting the On-Site Witness Test:**\n  1. Corrected Commissioning Checklist (`COMM-CHK-DARN-ELEM`) recording `CEL-2025-Q2` as the CEL edition consulted, documenting that `Arvexa PV-750` is not listed, and re-marking Section 6 from batch copy-forward `"Witness test: waiver eligible"` to `"Witness test required"` (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.1, §4.3`).\n  2. Confirmed construction-complete status (Checklist Sections 1–4 `Pass` as of `06/15/2025`), approved single-line diagram, and approved protection settings sheet on file (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2`).\n  3. Customer / commissioning agent's written `IEEE 1547.1` witness test plan, current calibration certificates/identifiers for test instrumentation, identification of qualified operating personnel, and test-plan/scheduling correspondence (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2, §4.3`).\n  4. Manufacturer's certificate of conformance / factory test report and technical datasheet for the `Arvexa PV-750` inverter (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.3`).\n- **Prior to SOC Release / PTO Issuance:**\n  1. Completed and signed Alleniom Witness Engineer test record with passing dispositions across all test points (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2, §4.3` — no post-PTO deferral or conditional PTO permitted).\n  2. Utility-owned RTU allocation, physical installation, communications path provisioning to SOC, and end-to-end SCADA point verification confirmed live at the SOC operator display by the SOC Shift Supervisor (`Lena Kovalchuk`) per `TCS-02 §3.6, §5` (Checklist Section 5 items 5.1–5.4 are currently `Pending`).\n\n**Parent Batch Case:** Work Package #45 (*Process the municipal witness-test waiver batch*).	2025-08-15	\N	1	11	9	5	4	0	\N	\N	2026-11-24 03:29:31.922528+00	2026-11-24 03:29:31.953433+00	2025-07-14	\N	\N	1	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	25	f	\N	\N	\N
48	1	3	Schedule on-site witness test — Holcott Public Library Array (510 kW, Selvix SV-720)	**Facility / Site:** Holcott Public Library Array (80 Old Mill Road, Holcott, Alleron 84HO; POI: Utility secondary, service transformer T-4)\n**Customer / Host:** Town of Holcott\n**Checklist Reference:** `Checklist_Holcott_Library.pdf` (`Doc no. CX-HOL-LIB-01`, Rev 0, dated `06/17/2025`; Field Engineer `M. Halbrook, P.E.`, badge `AFE-1042`, Alleniom Field Services Crew 12)\n**Nameplate Capacity & Class:** `510 kW` AC (Commercial small-scale DER, `500 kW – 1 MW`, `DIS-01 Rev 4` Table 3-1 / Table 5-1 Category 2)\n**Installed Inverter:** `Selvix SV-720`\n\n### 1. CEL Carriage & Waiver Eligibility Determination (`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §3, §4.1`)\n- **Call on Carriage:** **NOT CARRIED** on current Certified Equipment List `CEL-2025-Q2` (published `04/30/2025`, superseding `CEL-2024-Q4` of `10/31/2024`).\n- **Basis:** Although `Selvix SV-720` (720 kW central inverter, UL 1741-SB, effective `10/31/2024`) appeared on Row 29 of the Inverters tab of superseded `CEL-2024-Q4` (cited in Footnote 1 of `CX-HOL-LIB-01`), it was delisted/removed and not carried forward into `CEL-2025-Q2` (`CEL-2025-Q2` Front Matter Row 22 and Notes & Cross-References Rows 6–8). Under `ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §3` (Corollaries 1, 3, 4, and 5) and `§4.1`, listings appearing solely on a superseded CEL edition confer no waiver eligibility once the successor edition takes effect (flagged by Evan Solberg on commissioning wiki page `der-program/commissioning/municipal/checklist-holcott-library`).\n- **Disposition:** Ineligible for witness-test waiver. **On-site witness test required prior to Permission to Operate (PTO).**\n\n### 2. Tests to Be Performed and Basis (`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §4.2`)\nTesting shall be conducted on site per **`IEEE 1547.1`** and **`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §4.2`**, covering the requirements of **`DIS-01 Rev 4 §5 (Table 5-1 Category 2)` & `§6`**, **`IEEE 1547-2018 Clause 4`**, and **`DPS-07 Rev 2`**:\n1. **Protective-Function Trip Tests:** On-site verification of under-/over-voltage (`ANSI 27/59`) and under-/over-frequency (`ANSI 81U/81O`) trip pickup thresholds, clearing times, reconnect timing, overcurrent protection coordination with the utility feeder at service transformer T-4, and protective relay settings against the approved protection coordination study (Checklist Section B-1, B-2, B-4, B-5).\n2. **Anti-Islanding Function Test:** Unintentional islanding / loss-of-utility test per `IEEE 1547.1` confirming the `Selvix SV-720` ceases to energize and trips within the required `≤ 2.0 s` window (Checklist Section B-3).\n3. **Voltage and Frequency Ride-Through (VRT / FRT) Verifications:** Verification of programmed Category II voltage and frequency ride-through profiles (`DIS-01 Rev 4`) and reactive power / voltage support settings against the approved settings sheet (`DIS-01 Rev 4 §6`).\n\n### 3. Who Performs and Who Witnesses (`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §4.2, §4.3`)\n- **Scheduling / Coordination:** Alleniom Utilities DER Program Commissioning Coordinator schedules the earliest mutually available test date with the customer/commissioning agent and Alleniom witness engineer (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2`).\n- **Performed / Operated By:** Customer (**Town of Holcott**) and its qualified **Commissioning Agent / electrical contractor of record** (coordinated with field engineer `M. Halbrook, P.E.`, `AFE-1042`, Field Services Crew 12), who supply the written test plan, calibrated test instrumentation, and qualified personnel to operate the equipment (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2`).\n- **Witnessed, Recorded & Dispositioned By:** **Alleniom Utilities Witness Engineer** (**Standards Engineering** — `Evan Solberg` or designated Alleniom witness engineer), who observes on site, records calibrated instrument identifiers and measured values, assigns pass/fail dispositions per test point, and signs and dates the witness test record (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2, §4.3`).\n\n### 4. What Must Be on File First (`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §4.1–§4.3`, `TCS-02 §3.6, §5`)\n- **Prior to Conducting the On-Site Witness Test:**\n  1. Corrected Commissioning Checklist (`CX-HOL-LIB-01`) recording `CEL-2025-Q2` (`04/30/2025`) as the CEL edition consulted, documenting that `Selvix SV-720` was removed from `CEL-2025-Q2` (rendering the `CEL-2024-Q4` Footnote 1 reference ineligible under `ENG-PRC-014 §3`), re-marking Section F from `"Witness test: waiver eligible"` to `"Witness test: required — schedule with Standards Engineering"` (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.1, §4.3`), and completing the pending Field Services Supervisor sign-off block.\n  2. Confirmed construction-complete status (Checklist Sections A–D `Pass` as of `06/17/2025`, punch-list closed `06/12/2025`), approved single-line diagram, approved settings sheet, and approved protection coordination study on file (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2`).\n  3. Customer / commissioning agent's written `IEEE 1547.1` witness test plan, current calibration certificates/identifiers for test instrumentation, identification of qualified operating personnel, and test-plan/scheduling correspondence (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2, §4.3`).\n  4. Manufacturer's certificate of conformance / factory test report and technical documentation for the `Selvix SV-720` inverter (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.3`).\n- **Prior to SOC Release / PTO Issuance:**\n  1. Completed and signed Alleniom Witness Engineer test record with passing dispositions across all test points (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2, §4.3` — no post-PTO deferral or conditional PTO permitted).\n  2. Utility-owned RTU allocation, physical installation and enclosure sealing (Section E-1), fiber/cellular backhaul provisioning to SOC (Section E-2), and end-to-end SCADA signal verification with SOC (Section E-4) confirmed live at the SOC operator display by the SOC Shift Supervisor (`Lena Kovalchuk`) per `TCS-02 §3.6, §5` (Items E-1, E-2, and E-4 are currently `Pending`; Item E-3 point list submitted `06/10/2025` and Item E-5 revenue meter `S/N 44-118-7392` are `Pass`).\n\n**Parent 