49	1	3	Schedule on-site witness test — Lockmere Middle School Array (720 kW, Selvix SV-720)	**Facility / Site:** Lockmere Middle School Array (610 Chestnut Ridge Lane, Lockmere, Alleron 34LO; Application ID `PXA-2024-0793`; Feeder `ALN-152`)\n**Customer / Host:** Lockmere Community School District (`P. Ashworth`, Facilities Director, `(612) 555-0708`, `p.ashworth@lockmerecsd.org`)\n**Checklist & Wiki Record Reference:** `Checklist_Lockmere_Middle.pdf` (`Doc no. COMM-LKM-MS-2025-06`, Rev 0, dated `06/18/2025`; Commissioning Agent `K. Ondras`, Field Engineer `M. Halbrook, P.E.`) and DER Program Commissioning Wiki (`der-program/commissioning/municipal/checklist-lockmere-middle`, file note by Standards Engineer `Evan Solberg`)\n**Nameplate Capacity & Class:** `720 kW` AC (Commercial small-scale DER, `500 kW – 1 MW`, `DIS-01 Rev 4` Table 3-1 / Table 5-1 Category 2)\n**Installed Inverter:** `Selvix SV-720` (substituted on site after submission of the `06/18/2025` checklist, which still displays the originally specified `4 × Torvane Electric TE-180K` units)\n\n### 1. CEL Carriage & Waiver Eligibility Determination (`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §2, §3, §4.1`)\n- **Call on Carriage:** **NOT CARRIED** on current Certified Equipment List `CEL-2025-Q2` (published `04/30/2025`, superseding `CEL-2024-Q4` of `10/31/2024`).\n- **Basis:** While the originally filed `Torvane Electric TE-180K` (4 × 180 kW) shown on the unrevised `06/18/2025` checklist is listed on `CEL-2025-Q2` (Inverters tab, Row 14), the commissioning wiki record (`der-program/commissioning/municipal/checklist-lockmere-middle`, Comment ID 15 by Standards Engineer `Evan Solberg`) establishes that **"the inverter installed at Lockmere Middle is a Selvix SV-720. It was substituted on site after this checklist was submitted and the checklist still shows the original unit."** Under `ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §2`, `§3` (Corollary 2: every inverter actually installed at the facility must appear on the current CEL edition), and `§4.1`, waiver eligibility is determined by the equipment **actually installed on site** (`Selvix SV-720`). `Selvix SV-720` appeared only on superseded `CEL-2024-Q4` (Inverters tab, Row 29) and was delisted/removed from current `CEL-2025-Q2` (`ENG-PRC-014 §3` Corollaries 1, 3, 5).\n- **Disposition:** Ineligible for witness-test waiver. **On-site witness test of the installed `Selvix SV-720` is required prior to Permission to Operate (PTO).**\n\n### 2. Tests to Be Performed and Basis (`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §2, §4.2`)\nBecause all Section 2 and Section 3 verifications on `COMM-LKM-MS-2025-06` (`06/18/2025`) were recorded against the replaced `Torvane Electric TE-180K` units (S/N `TE180K-24-11482 / -11487 / -11491 / -11502`, FW `4.11.02`), full on-site witness testing of the substituted **`Selvix SV-720`** must be conducted per **`IEEE 1547.1`** and **`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §2 & §4.2`**, covering **`DIS-01 Rev 4 §5 (Table 5-1 Category 2)` & `§6`**, **`IEEE 1547-2018 Clause 4`**, **`DPS-07 Rev 2`**, and **`TCS-02 §3.3(a), §3.6, §5`**:\n1. **Protective-Function Trip Tests on Substituted `Selvix SV-720`:** On-site verification of protective relay and inverter trip elements (`ANSI 27/59` under-/over-voltage: `27` at 0.88 pu / 2.0 s, `59` at 1.10 pu / 1.0 s and 1.20 pu / 0.16 s; `ANSI 81U/81O` under-/over-frequency: `81U` at 58.5 Hz / 2.0 s, `81O` at 61.2 Hz / 2.0 s; `ANSI 25` sync; `ANSI 32` directional power), reconnect delay timing, DER breaker local and remote trip from the `Selvix SV-720` auxiliary relay, and utility POI recloser reclose-block interlock coordination with the DER breaker status contact (Checklist Sections 2 & 3).\n2. **Anti-Islanding Function Test on Substituted `Selvix SV-720`:** Unintentional islanding / open-utility test per `IEEE 1547.1` confirming passive + active anti-islanding detection and trip within the required `≤ 2.0 s` window (Checklist Sections 2 & 3).\n3. **Voltage and Frequency Ride-Through (VRT / FRT) & Telemetry Gateway Verifications:** Verification of programmed Category II, Region III voltage and frequency ride-through profiles against the approved settings sheet (`DIS-01 Rev 4 §6`), together with verification that utility-owned RTU `RTU-LKM-171-04` polls and reports valid live data points from the substituted `Selvix SV-720` inverter/gateway to SOC SCADA per `TCS-02 §3.3(a), §3.6, §5, §6`.\n\n### 3. Who Performs and Who Witnesses (`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §4.2, §4.3`)\n- **Scheduling / Coordination:** Alleniom Utilities DER Program Commissioning Coordinator schedules the earliest mutually available test date with the customer/commissioning agent and Alleniom witness engineer (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2`).\n- **Performed / Operated By:** Customer (**Lockmere Community School District**, `P. Ashworth`, Facilities Director, `(612) 555-0708`) and its qualified **Commissioning Agent / contractor of record** (coordinated with commissioning agent `K. Ondras`, Field Services, and field engineer `M. Halbrook, P.E.`, `AFE-1042`), who supply the written test plan, calibrated test instrumentation, and qualified personnel to operate the equipment (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2`).\n- **Witnessed, Recorded & Dispositioned By:** **Alleniom Utilities Witness Engineer** (**Standards Engineering** — `Evan Solberg` or designated Alleniom witness engineer), who observes on site, records calibrated instrument identifiers and measured values, assigns pass/fail dispositions per test point, and signs and dates the witness test record (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2, §4.3`).\n\n### 4. What Must Be on File First (`ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §2, §4.1–§4.3`, `DIS-01 Rev 4 §7`, `TCS-02 §3.6, §5`)\n- **Prior to Conducting the On-Site Witness Test:**\n  1. **ISA Equipment-Substitution Change Order & As-Built Package (`DIS-01 Rev 4 §7`):** Written ISA change-order documentation covering the post-execution substitution of `1 × Selvix SV-720` (720 kW) for `4 × Torvane Electric TE-180K` (720 kW) within the same 720 kW nameplate capacity rating and same POI on Feeder `ALN-152` (permitted under `DIS-01 Rev 4 §7`, *Other post-execution changes*), along with updated as-built single-line diagrams, equipment schedule, and O&M documentation.\n  2. **Revised Commissioning Checklist (`COMM-LKM-MS-2025-06`):** Updated checklist replacing the `Torvane Electric TE-180K` model, serial numbers (`TE180K-24-11482 / -11487 / -11491 / -11502`), firmware (`Torvane FW 4.11.02`), and `CEL-2025-Q2` listing citation in Sections 2, 3, and 7 with the actually installed `Selvix SV-720` serial number(s), firmware version, and approved settings sheet, and re-marking Sections 7 and 9 from `"Witness test: waiver eligible"` to `"Witness test: witness attendance required"` / Waiver Denied (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.1, §4.3`).\n  3. **Test Plan & Instrumentation Credentials (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2, §4.3`):** Customer / commissioning agent's written `IEEE 1547.1` witness test plan for the `Selvix SV-720`, current calibration certificates/identifiers for test instrumentation, identification of qualified operating personnel, and scheduling correspondence.\n  4. **Manufacturer Documentation (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.3`):** Manufacturer's certificate of conformance, factory test report, and approved protection settings sheet for the `Selvix SV-720`.\n- **Prior to SOC Release / PTO Issuance:**\n  1. Completed and signed Alleniom Witness Engineer test record with passing dispositions across all test points on the installed `Selvix SV-720` (`ENG-PRC-014 §4.2, §4.3` — no post-PTO deferral or conditional PTO permitted).\n  2. Confirmation with SOC (`Lena Kovalchuk`, SOC Shift Supervisor) and SCADA/EMS Engineering (`Marcus Deele`) that utility RTU `RTU-LKM-171-04` (installed `06/12/2025` and verified `06/17/2025` under SCADA ticket `TKT-25-04188` prior to the post-submission inverter substitution notice) is actively polling the substituted `Selvix SV-720` gateway and presenting valid, non-stale live points at the SOC SCADA display at the time PTO is requested (`TCS-02 §3.3(a), §3.6, §5`).\n\n**Parent Batch Case:** Work Package #45 (*Process the municipal witness-test waiver batch*).	2025-08-15	\N	1	11	9	5	4	0	\N	\N	2026-11-24 03:29:34.000103+00	2026-11-24 03:29:34.022661+00	2025-07-14	\N	\N	1	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	25	f	\N	\N	\N
